SUMMARY:L’Alliance New York Announces 2026 French Summer Camps & Classes Manhattan & Montclair\, NJ Campuses
DESCRIPTION:Join L’Alliance New York at French Camp this summer at its Manhattan and Montclair campuses. Running for nine weeks from late June through late August\, L’Alliance offers one of the longest and most affordable French immersion camp experiences in the New York area. This year\, children of all ages and levels of French dive into the world of art in all its forms—from music and theater to visual arts and movement—all in French. Older students extend their learning through inspiring cultural experiences across New York City for Manhattan campers\, and throughout Montclair and the surrounding area for Montclair campers. Enroll now for an adventure your child won’t want to miss. Weekday classes (45 to 90 minutes) are also offered for young children—ages 1–5 in Manhattan and ages 1–7 in Montclair (Saturdays only)—as well as week-long French immersion programs for teens (ages 11–18) at both campuses. 5% sibling and 10% multiple-week discounts are available.\nL’Alliance New York – Manhattan Campus • 22 E. 60th Street • Phone: 646-388-6612 • Email: languagecenter@lallianceny.org\nL’Alliance New York – Montclair Campus • 17–19 Munn Street • Phone: 973-783-0507 • Email: montclair@lallianceny.org\nMore information and summer camp/class registration is available here.\n*5% Early Bird discount available only on summer camps and classes. Not offered on private lessons. Can not be combined with other discounts except the $25 Refer-a-Friend\, 10% multiple-week discount\, and 5% sibling discounts. Excludes books & other materials. Discount expires at 11:59pm ET\, Sunday\, May 31\, 2026.\nManhattan Campus:\nSummer Day Camps\nJun 22—Aug 21\n1-week sessions\nFor Toddlers Ages 3-5 (Pre-K) | Mon-Fri\, 9am–12pm • 9am–4pm\nFor Kids Ages 5-11 (Grades K-5) | Mon-Fri\, 9am–4pm\nChildren ages 3 to 5 will discover different artistic disciplines by exploring a variety of themes: music\, painting\, sculpture\, theater\, cinema\, fashion\, photography\, dance… and much more\, during 9 weeks of creativity and fun!\nOlder children will also have the opportunity to explore these same themes through outings in New York City\, a true cultural hub of international renown. Enjoy an artistic and urban adventure that promises wonderful memories and many discoveries!\nLearn more here.\nSummer French Classes\nJun 22—Aug 29\n5-week sessions\nFor Toddlers Ages 1-5\nMon-Fri\, once per week\, 45–90 min\nOpen to all levels\, these engaging sessions use activities\, games\, and dynamic lessons designed for young learners. They’re ideal for families wanting to boost their child’s French skills while keeping the experience enjoyable.\nFind a class here.\nTeens Immersion Classes\nJun 22—Aug 21\n1-week sessions\nFor Teens Ages 11-18\nMon-Fri\, 9:30am–12:30pm\nL’Alliance’s Teen Immersion Classes are perfect for teens aiming to enhance their French skills. Meeting daily for 3 hours\, these classes cater to all proficiency levels and focus on speaking\, listening\, reading\, and writing through interactive activities. This program is ideal for students preparing for high school exams or seeking personal growth in French.\nLearn more here.\nAdditional Programming in Manhattan\nSpring Youth Classes\nMon\, Mar 30—Mon\, Jun 8\n10-week session\nChildren learn French naturally through stories\, songs\, games\, crafts\, and movement. Classes are guided by native-speaking teachers and include fun\, immersive activities designed to build confidence\, vocabulary\, and fluency at every level.\nFind a class here.\nCned Program\nExpert Tutoring for Native French-Speaking Children\n2026-2027 school year registrations now open\nEarly Bird priority discount ends April 30.\nOffered at L’Alliance’s Manhattan and Montclair campuses\, this in-person program\, developed in partnership with Cned\, is designed for French-speaking children—or those with an equivalent level of proficiency—ages 5–14 (Grades K–8). Led by qualified teachers in small group settings\, the program provides a structured and engaging learning experience aligned with the French national curriculum. It supports the development of strong academic skills in French\, including reading\, writing\, and communication\, while fostering intellectual rigor and a lasting connection to the French language.\nVirtual information sessions are held on the last Thursday of each month\, from January to June\, from 12:30pm to 1:30pm. Click here to register for an information session\,\nLearn more here\, or register here for the 2026-2027 school year.\nL’Alliance Preschool – Manhattan Upper East Side Campus\nFrench Immersion Program\nAges 2 ½ to 5\nL’Alliance Preschool is a French-immersion program for toddlers ages 2 ½ to 5 located on the Upper East Side of Manhattan\, and Montclair\, New Jersey. Surrounded by French throughout the day\, children grow naturally in their ability to understand\, speak\, and think in the language as they play\, explore\, and discover the world around them. Designed to spark curiosity and a love of learning\, L’Alliance Preschool is open to all children regardless of their prior exposure to the French language.\nNow accepting applications\nFor school years 2026-2027 & 2027-2028\nRegister for an information session or book a private tour here.\nMontclair\, NJ Campus:\nSummer Day Camps\nJun 22—Aug 21\n1-week sessions\nFor Toddlers Ages 3-5 (Pre-K)\, Kids Ages 5-11 (Grades K-5)\nMon-Fri\, 8:30am–12:30pm • 8:30am–3:30pm\nExtended care is available until 6pm\nChildren ages 3 to 11 will discover different artistic disciplines by exploring a variety of themes: music\, painting\, sculpture\, theater\, cinema\, fashion\, photography\, dance… and much more —all in French!\nBuilding on the success of last year’s program\, we are again incorporating weekly field trips for our older campers (Ages 5-11 • Grades K-5) extending the immersive experience beyond the classroom and connecting artistic exploration with local cultural institutions. Planned outings include visits to: Montclair Art Museum\, Morris Museum\, Wildflower Sculpture Park\, Paterson Museum\, Montclair Public Library\, Van Vleck House & Gardens!\nLearn more here.\nSaturday Classes\nJun 27—Aug 29\n5 & 10-week sessions\nFor Toddlers Ages 1-5\, Kids Ages 5-7\nSat\, once per week\, 60–90 min\nOpen to all levels\, these engaging sessions use activities\, games\, and dynamic lessons designed for young learners. They’re ideal for families wanting to boost their child’s French skills while keeping the experience enjoyable. Classes for children aged 12–14 months are offered as “Toddler & Me” sessions\, in which a caregiver attends alongside the child. Programs for children aged 3½ to 5 and up are drop-off only. For children aged 2 to 3½\, both formats are available\, with options for either drop-off or “Toddler & Me” sessions.\nFind a class here.\nTeens Immersion Classes\nJun 22—Aug 21\n1-week sessions\nFor Teens Ages 11-18\nMon-Fri\, 9:45am–12:45pm\nL’Alliance’s Teen Immersion Classes are perfect for teens aiming to enhance their French skills. Meeting daily for 3 hours\, these classes cater to all proficiency levels and focus on speaking\, listening\, reading\, and writing through interactive activities. This program is ideal for students preparing for high school exams or seeking personal growth in French.\nLearn more here.\nAdditional Programming in Montclair\nSpring Youth Classes\nMon\, Mar 30—Mon\, Jun 8\n10-week session\nFor Toddlers Ages 1-5\, Kids & Teens Ages 5-18\nWeekdays and Saturdays\, once per week\, 60–90 min\nFrom playful first steps to advanced skills\, our programs adapt to each student’s level. Guided by native-speaking teachers and fun\, immersive activities designed to build confidence\, vocabulary\, and fluency at every level. Toddler classes available in both “Toddler & Me” and drop-off formats.\nFind a class here.\nCned Program\nExpert Tutoring for Native French-Speaking Children\n2026-2027 school year registrations now open\nEarly Bird priority discount ends April 30.\nOffered at L’Alliance’s Manhattan and Montclair campuses\, this in-person program\, developed in partnership with Cned\, is designed for French-speaking children—or those with an equivalent level of proficiency—ages 5–14 (Grades K–8). Led by qualified teachers in small group settings\, the program provides a structured and engaging learning experience aligned with the French national curriculum. It supports the development of strong academic skills in French\, including reading\, writing\, and communication\, while fostering intellectual rigor and a lasting connection to the French language.\nVirtual information sessions are held on the last Thursday of each month\, from January to June\, from 12:30pm to 1:30pm. Click here to register for an information session\,\nLearn more here\, or register here for the 2026-2027 school year.\nL’Alliance Preschool – Montclair Campus\nFrench Immersion Program\nAges 2 1/2 to 5\nL’Alliance Preschool is a French-immersion program for toddlers ages 2 ½ to 5 located in the Upper East Side of Manhattan\, and Montclair\, New Jersey. Surrounded by French throughout the day\, children grow naturally in their ability to understand\, speak\, and think in the language as they play\, explore\, and discover the world around them. Designed to spark curiosity and a love of learning\, L’Alliance Preschool is open to all children regardless of their prior exposure to the French language.\nNow accepting applications\nFor school years 2026-2027 & 2027-2028\nRegister for an information session or book a private tour here.\nAbout L’Alliance New York\nAttracting over 150\,000 visitors annually\, L’Alliance New York is the city’s premier center for French language and francophone arts and cultures. As an independent\, not-for-profit organization\, L’Alliance New York’s mission is to enrich everyday lives with the spirit of joie de vivre through education\, language\, and culture. L’Alliance New York is proud to provide its members and students with engaging French language classes and audacious multi-disciplinary programming that celebrates the diversity of francophone cultures and creativity around the world. L’Alliance New York is internationally known for offering the largest selection of fully-immersive French language courses for students aged one to 101\, and for its renowned cultural programming including the annual Bastille Day celebration that takes place on New York’s famed Madison Avenue\, attracting over 50\,000 visitors each year; the Crossing The Line arts and performance festival that engages NYC cultural institutions in bringing dynamic international artists to audiences; Animation First\, the biggest animation festival in the U.S; and the Comic Arts Fest\, celebrating the intersection of American and francophone comic arts. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/lalliance-new-york-announces-2026-french-summer-camps-classes-manhattan-montclair-nj-campuses/
LOCATION:L’Alliance New York Montclair Campus\, 17-19 Munn St\, 2nd Floor\, Montclair\, 07042\, United States
