SUMMARY:Young Innovators STEM Program
DESCRIPTION:Young Innovators is a hands-on STEM program designed for students in grades 3rd – 7th who are curious\, creative\, and excited to explore the worlds of engineering and technology. It will be a 2-week program\, and it is $60/week. \nWeek 1 will be ‘Engineering in Action\,’ where students take on engaging engineering challenges through LEGO design\, bridge-building competitions\, and Rube Goldberg machine projects. Along the way\, they learn how engineers use creativity\, critical thinking\, and problem-solving to develop solutions for real-world challenges. \nWeek 2 will be ‘Coding and Game design\,’ where students dive into computer science by learning the fundamentals of coding while designing and creating their own video games. This experience introduces programming concepts in a fun\, interactive\, and accessible way. \nThroughout the program\, Young Innovators encourages creativity\, collaboration\, critical thinking\, and innovation in an engaging\, hands-on environment. Whether they’re building\, designing\, or coding\, every participant leaves with new skills\, greater confidence\, and a deeper appreciation for STEM. \nWe are proud to be supporting access to education! A percentage of our proceeds will be donated to this important cause! \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
